          'In the Mexica account recorded by Sahagun, Coatlicue sweeps on Coatepec when a ball of feathers descends. She places it against her breast; the feathers disappear, and she becomes pregnant. Her daughter Coyolxauhqui regards this as a disgrace and gathers her four hundred brothers to climb the mountain and kill their mother.',
