          'The victorious prince eventually rules as Pachacuti, reshaping Cusco and directing further conquests. The expanding state and its ruler are subjects of historical investigation. Stones entering battle and divine selection of a successor belong to royal sacred narrative. These forms of memory interact, but they cannot be used as if they were identical evidence.'
